0..74 Comment "// A bridge `Bridge(A, a, b)` relates two points of `A` parametrically, as"
75..104 Comment "// the bridge fold reads `A`."
105..107 Comment "//"
108..184 Comment "// A path identifies its endpoints, and a bridge only relates them. A bridge"
185..261 Comment "// at the universe is a relation between two types, and one at a type former"
262..337 Comment "// lifts the relations of its parts. A bridge has no reflexivity, transport"
338..366 Comment "// or eliminator of its own."
367..369 Comment "//"
370..448 Comment "// An introduction checked at a bridge checks at the fibre the fold reads from"
449..525 Comment "// the carrier and the endpoints. The fold reads a list cell by cell, a base"
526..601 Comment "// type or a sum as its identity, and a function code by extensionality. An"
602..656 Comment "// atom stating an identity system bears its relation."
657..659 Comment "//"
660..730 Comment "// - see: `pathological/identity/bridge.gandr` — the bridges refused"
731..777 Comment "// - see: #3519 — the model laws of the fold"
778..848 Comment "// - see: Cavallo and Harper, _Internal parametricity for cubical type"
849..878 Comment "//   theory_, LMCS 2021, § 3"
880..934 Comment "// The sealed points whose relation is their identity."
